2a59cc2a-02c1-5501-be18-04bcc0a03c49" :question/math-academy-id "q-94062" :question/problem "Which of the following could be matrices of quadratic forms defined on ${R}^{3}?$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -8 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that every quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ has an associated $3\\times 3$ symmetric matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $T$ could be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ since it is a $3\\times 3$ symmetric matrix.\n\n- $U$ could also be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ since it is a $3\\times 3$ symmetric matrix.\n\n- $V$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ since it's a $2\\times 2$ matrix (not $3\\times 3$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$T$ and $U$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94062/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e62e458d-0724-5dbe-b448-b79404f279f9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94062"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186162518 :question/answer-fields 17592186160740] {:db/id "q-93700/selection/ma-v1/6b9b7ce9df843cb9f4c36d46291d40e6a7f33e2555dffd7986cc2abb51a4e2e1/f6ed8c3e8ac11c4c476e856e67261d9addd41c460d2f0404e6d3f3a72ad0633a" :answer/id #uuid "37c2ac69-1dd2-59dc-9509-5e16d930d734" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93700/selection/ma-v1/6b9b7ce9df843cb9f4c36d46291d40e6a7f33e2555dffd7986cc2abb51a4e2e1/5f6c142a82c4a0bf971b412708f6830f8e50a71860d9c4cebbd361a473710cf0" :answer/id #uuid "ee9a4534-ef46-54ed-ab3c-5ff1b11bf4f3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93700/sele