 {:db/id "q-94059" :question/id #uuid "76222307-a5b8-5a1d-9d57-08bb293d8059" :question/math-academy-id "q-94059" :question/problem "Which of the following could be matrices of quadratic forms defined on ${R}^{2}?$\n\n$$\nK=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,L=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,M=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that every quadratic form defined on ${R}^{2}$ has an associated $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $K$ could be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{2}$ since it is a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\n- $L$ could also be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{2}$ since it is a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\n- $M$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{2}.$ Although it's a $2\\times 2$ matrix, $M$ is not symmetric since ${m}_{12}\\ne {m}_{21}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$K$ and $L$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94059/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e62e458d-0724-5dbe-b448-b79404f279f9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94059"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94086/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "f9a61166-3797-5460-8c56-46d77cacfd89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94086/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "a0987f74-3140-5562-8061-a25b731c989b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94086/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "0ef3d559-08f5-5bb6-bde6-95b7cefa5705" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94086/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "15dd36b5-0cbe-5b23-b001-a0b53127c5cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94086/selection/4b741b651b6f24cd7370ee85fd4c2dd5b1d9bdb7c612965a77adc26bd59b4a9a" :answer/id #uuid "91cdd038-19c9-5d17-8cf4-a7ed07e565e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "41" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94086/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3bd68df-2125-5ea7-83c3-c4d3505e1836" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94086/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer-field/choices ["q-94086/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-94086/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" "q-94086/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-94086/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" "q-94086/selection/4b741b651b6f24cd7370ee85fd4c2dd5b1d9bdb7c612965a77adc26bd59b4a9a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94086" :question/id #uuid "471337b8-f399-528b-a6f9-2aa14b02c489" :question/math-academy-id "q-94086" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}^{T}\\,Ax$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ into the expression for $Q(x),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94086/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90f62dc8-396d-5f7f-8295-2e7b5d62bd78"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94086"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-93703"] :question/problem "Consider the quadratic form \n$Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3}^{2}.$ \nEvaluate $Q(x)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the expression for $Q(x)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={1}^{2}-3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-4)-0\\cdot (-4)+(-4)^{2} \\\\  & =1+12+0+16 \\\\  & =29.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-94087/selection/ebe3072a1dd0240f82f7c04e06603ef971401ed1aea6a421c38664ef5adb09f3" :answer/id #uuid "7df437cb-7ab5-5d04-abec-f4a4e0623be5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "29" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94087/selection/0b264a929df91f183c31537acf560edd2114ab983879cbe61ea3aed58b55bda9" :answer/id #uuid "4ddfe168-f394-500f-8d06-64f7491338ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "55" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94087/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer/id #uuid "ce66e990-4984-5b7c-ab66-d3665ecdc061" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94087/selection/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" :answer/id #uuid "fc23782d-feb4-517b-afae-108b72298938" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "65" :db/ensure [:answer/va