:db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94105" :question/id #uuid "fa520ceb-dcfd-527f-b050-d283d140e1ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-94105" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{2}+(-1){x}_{2}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+(-1){x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1})+{x}_{2}(2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})+{x}_{3}(-{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94105/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94105"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94091/selection/c0b171489bf956ba196d6b4789b252e96eeed9645cb3afc9521484eb4bc0e26f" :answer/id #uuid "6078ce66-cc65-5238-949b-cb37333f23f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94091/selection/84e0844e83b3d372e08b54e45885eb24eb25cabfff2f275ad9d391f655aca7f8" :answer/id #uuid "adca5736-1860-5983-a98b-1419a6564f8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94091/selection/901ad2329c759d44ee3e2b8d2b5e971049bc59d9b407e714dd98f2926215408c" :answer/id #uuid "ce00ad34-5906-5dfd-9954-4c5b24ff47d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94091/selection/762d33960e82042677bba2eca0c976dc30262ab92a05343e431fbd398cf6c832" :answer/id #uuid "d25da20c-d3ef-5fc8-81ba-05bd7f23f551" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94091/selection/8360fb57d435e669a9ecd3a22578509a02d20c68816ebd66f91696f79ac92aca" :answer/id #uuid "6c0fa134-0e34-5018-8a25-496d643a4d2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94091/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa103db-8fe3-5e4f-8786-3e8e80d954e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94091/selection/762d33960e82042677bba2eca0c976dc30262ab92a05343e431fbd398cf6c832" :answer-field/choices ["q-94091/selection/c0b171489bf956ba196d6b4789b252e96eeed9645cb3afc9521484eb4bc0e26f" "q-94091/selection/84e0844e83b3d372e08b54e45885eb24eb25cabfff2f275ad9d391f655aca7f8" "q-94091/selection/901ad2329c759d44ee3e2b8d2b5e971049bc59d9b407e714dd98f2926215408c" "q-94091/selection/762d33960e82042677bba2eca0c976dc30262ab92a05343e431fbd398cf6c832" "q-94091/selection/8360fb57d435e669a9ecd3a22578509a02d20c68816ebd66f91696f79ac92aca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94091" :question/id #uuid "ca279526-b62e-56f6-bb58-940f0a3d4e3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-94091" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =2{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(-4){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-4){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94091/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94091"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140928/selection/1f995a54c0f6e749e7e51fdd9bb78b3de3e9199d6bab32ce47cc0640c94390ce" :answer/id #uuid "cd8cbfee-e53b-501e-a2a3-25444ae58ebf" :answer/type :answe