d "q-140928" :question/id #uuid "4a4aa31a-9bd3-531e-9d58-38401292e334" :question/math-academy-id "q-140928" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-1){x}_{1}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+(-1){x}_{3}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1}-{x}_{3})+{x}_{2}(3{x}_{3})+{x}_{3}(-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140928/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140928"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94093/selection/5279d1159e1ac2bbbd6606a3b1081c3058ff093ecaf2d1f3e599d88d8911bc10" :answer/id #uuid "443c69da-b249-5213-9d76-08b710b0adb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94093/selection/3217846c092c47173d9f73bb709157e93eabd4d03d0ba7487c22b563af394edf" :answer/id #uuid "ab2d495e-83ac-563a-923b-53a5c84064b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94093/selection/d00d96c774868797bdacbc548e233371c273b2b7878304b9ff6aa3b27fb40393" :answer/id #uuid "4de100ce-2821-5bc3-97a8-6959a5be99f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94093/selection/476592f0dc8adb749c11d68b4d80173095155fae51d5d846f79c971897ca1b81" :answer/id #uuid "e80e3f9b-abf4-5061-a3cb-cb6a316f512a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94093/selection/4c569ce37fd875e78f2593145a24223c78b528d1eccb5fae43dab3dfed7760a0" :answer/id #uuid "7b822a13-e1cd-5b45-a763-dea8f050c727" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94093/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb8504f8-efb6-527b-a920-e7711490f632" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94093/selection/3217846c092c47173d9f73bb709157e93eabd4d03d0ba7487c22b563af394edf" :answer-field/choices ["q-94093/selection/5279d1159e1ac2bbbd6606a3b1081c3058ff093ecaf2d1f3e599d88d8911bc10" "q-94093/selection/3217846c092c47173d9f73bb709157e93eabd4d03d0ba7487c22b563af394edf" "q-94093/selection/d00d96c774868797bdacbc548e233371c273b2b7878304b9ff6aa3b27fb40393" "q-94093/selection/476592f0dc8adb749c11d68b4d80173095155fae51d5d846f79c971897ca1b81" "q-94093/selection/4c569ce37fd875e78f2593145a24223c78b528d1eccb5fae43dab3dfed7760a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94093" :question/id #uuid "bc073d63-fb25-5413-bfbf-32bd918e2a6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-94093" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =2{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(3){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(3){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}(3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94093/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94093"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94097/selection/b00a598388d37585988d52921aea4cdb8d74937142bcb303ddff0315f1e3280a" :answer/id #uuid "fcc25e35-105d-50c5-903d-d3f8deeea081" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94097/selection/aa3d42b4fde5cb2ade6ded8d70c7c3222be5de99d2b0d4b1b96739c4a0dee51b" :answer/id #uuid "603edd03-6654-55e1-a27b-c98cc1588875" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94097/selection/fe3bcc9bddd6a83e82428a21b6ccdd7f89ecb7a2d41c186d220aef15b673f27d" :answer/id #uuid "4ef13af9-e8e5-580d-8dba-52d8cfa05f59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94097/selection/754e376b907c16489d7345e1627ba46e7b3153f10d89d1478734b2b1bffd249e" :answer/id #uuid "22e05f01-6033-53e4-9bf4-c9988ba8813a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94097/selection/55b50308ca0f799092909994ff309c826ec34f48943c3c692dcf7f327f13bd9e" :answer/id #uuid "16295f87-f043-5952-9837-8078f1fd4b3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94097/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "186fcce2-a80a-55cf-a52e-be3e630037e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94097/selection/b00a598388d37585988d52921aea4cdb8d74937142bcb303ddff0315f1e3280a" :answer-field/choices ["q-94097/selection/b00a598388d37585988d52921aea4cdb8d74937142bcb303ddff0315f1e3280a" "q-94097/selection/aa3d42b4fde5cb2ade6ded8d70c7c3222be5de99d2b0d4b1b96739c4a0dee51b" "q-94097/selection/fe3bcc9bddd6a83e82428a21b6ccdd7f89ecb7a2d41c186d220aef15b673f27d" "q-94097/selection/754e376b907c16489d7345e1627ba46e7b3153f10d89d1478734b2b1bffd249e" "q-94097/selection/55b50308ca0f799092909994ff309c826ec34f48943c3c692dcf7f327f13bd9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94097" :question/id #uuid "f71c8acd-e0e8-5ba6-aaaa-b92c7ebe1f3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94097" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+1{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+1{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1}+{x}_{3})+{x}_{2}({x}_{2})+{x}_{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94097/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94097"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94115/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "038cdf04-77a7-58e9-b409-e9bef0ad24fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94115/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "056015f0-7d16-5ce3-b267-b04635ba752d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94115/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "48349de2-172f-555d-9f36-f639631e6ec8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94115/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "5cbc3c5f-0d0f-5b40-b202-79d411761490" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94115/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "2f11831a-adf6-54e9-864b-37bbc5b01056" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94115/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0bd1b039-6ff2-5677-b5d9-c6b88d9fc65c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94115/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-94115/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-94115/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-94115/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-94115/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-94115/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94115" :question/id #uuid "c483845a-2df2-5f96-9a60-d364acbd9e17" :question/math-academy-id "q-94115" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & b \\\\ b & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ is given above. What is the value of $b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,1{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+(-2){x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must split the coefficient of $2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries \n\n$$\n{a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{2}{2}=1\n$$\n\nof our matrix. So, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b=1$ and $c=-2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\nb+c=1-2=-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94115/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94115"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140932/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "3979a24d-dd44-5002-a16a-2afe4b43c2c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140932/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "c8bbc316-0329-531a-98a4-1a3e1f8a28c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140932/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "d34bd976-257d-5945-8a50-eceb2a407ede" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140932/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "ccc39b96-a204-55cf-ac76-e3eb2a9b4929" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140932/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "56d51bb0-20f2-57c0-a14e-dc4c879af00c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140932/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dedf6fd6-47a3-5036-97a0-506ab279bd4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140932/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-140932/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-140932/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-140932/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-140932/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-140932/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140932" :question/id #uuid "46502b93-4d5f-5b44-a9ca-d570ed1198d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-140932" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ b & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+(-2){x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,(-2){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must split the coefficient of $-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries \n\n$$\n{a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{(-4)}{2}=-2\n$$\n\nof our matrix. So, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2$ and $b=-2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=2+(-2)=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140932/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140932"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94117/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "c838e8e0-61e6-5e60-992a-6525732217bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94117/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "ba0d6865-12de-5d9d-a477-0a9ebe66afd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94117/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "cd1cdb0d-2b51-545f-9cf2-3d813f766c15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94117/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "489266df-1d0d-55db-b1cf-815a04a49632" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94117/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "39114c83-642b-5d04-971f-869f3c2701c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94117/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b53e7f8-75d3-51ee-8786-fd4ba3663cc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94117/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-94117/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-94117/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-94117/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-94117/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-94117/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94117" :question/id #uuid "48eb3bee-71af-55b4-ac22-cbdbf3fba67b" :question/math-academy-id "q-94117" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 1 & b \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-5){x}_{1}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,1{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}^{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,(-5){x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must do the following splits:\n\n- we split the coefficient of $2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries ${a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{2}{2}=1,$ and\n\n- we split the coefficient of $-10{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ between the entries ${a}_{13}={a}_{31}=\\frac{-10}{2}=-5.$\n\nSo, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3,$ $b=-5,$ and $c=3.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=3+(-5)+3=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-94117/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94117"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94113/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "fd023245-7d38-5d14-8c27-987720c5b682" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94113/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "468de98b-2887-587d-a6fa-08d26cc2698f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94113/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "b228d77c-27e0-5201-9c57-5006fcd29a51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94113/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "e0ccb8f0-378b-5d03-9301-84e98e4ead04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94113/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "2a372720-df66-53cc-b3f0-60ca15197bd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94113/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "003f5cc2-2265-518b-ada2-7b58607dfed3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94113/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-94113/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-94113/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-94113/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-94113/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-94113/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94113" :question/id #uuid "1963362a-57e4-5a67-b932-bddf81aa4778" :question/math-academy-id "q-94113" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & b \\\\ b & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ is given above. What is the value of $b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}^{2}+(-3){x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,(-3){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must split the coefficient of $-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries \n\n$$\n{a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{-6}{2}=-3\n$$\n\nof our matrix. So, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b=-3$ and $c=1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\nb+c=-3+1=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94113/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94113"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94120/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ad421802-26c1-5213-a10b-0799186bb9f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94120/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "6abcc35c-70c0-5fa1-a95f-2a4fb9fa1d6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94120/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "35b4cf85-c620-50e4-95c9-bf79b02d4f7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94120/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "aa7617e3-4e91-534b-9b04-ad0ec22a32cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94120/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "9584e14a-6f16-5a85-b581-df59746a2262" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94120/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9445d247-8f3a-5484-a910-6509dafb73e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94120/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-94120/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-94120/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-94120/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-94120/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-94120/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94120" :question/id #uuid "073c0684-1181-52f2-8694-1c9e7ffaf10c" :question/math-academy-id "q-94120" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & b \\\\ 6 & a & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-2){x}_{1}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,6{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}^{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,(-2){x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must do the following splits:\n\n- we split the coefficient of $12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries ${a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{12}{2}=6,$ and\n\n- we split the coefficient of $-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ between the entries ${a}_{13}={a}_{31}=\\frac{-4}{2}=-2.$\n\nSo, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=0.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-2)+0=-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-94120/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94120"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8168"] :question/problem "Which of the following could be matrices of quadratic forms defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/e51c52e07d49052f578138e5c1d7e9f84a95ba8c454e7fcf834dcc9047dad432.png)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that every quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2$ has an associated $2 \\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $L$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2$ since it's a $3 \\times 3$ matrix (not $2 \\times 2$).\n\n- $M$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2.$  Although it's a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, $M$ is not symmetric since $m_{12} \\neq m_{21}.$\n\n- $N$ could be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2$ since it is a $2 \\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$N$ only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8169"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/791b214858b7ff88b6ad1ba98ea8336abbd678ffb34751b041e11cec8cd44143.png)\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{x}$ when ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/b7df527ba563debac29dbdd838aadb4f219653a77077b70b65bdbfe579e26a0a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Substituting ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/1a8e02bec4af0b88d7fa0f4cd87b9e0f89757ca87f494e1451650ac4f3a06dcf.png) into the expression for $Q(\\mathbf{x}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 23\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =86.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8170"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/59d795aef27f3ae7598e1a8503ba0dbde377486b355e0db6decc4753f9ae7544.png)\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which expression represents the corresponding quadratic form $\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{x}$ in terms of the components of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/31a4a301bddfd7435f188f76c1702beb7c2eea01a1b174d5195f321cfdef3103.png)" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry $a_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term $a_{ij}x_i x_j$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =-1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(1){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(1){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+-1{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8171"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/1bd9859db9b628b26d250310d38222e8d1474cbfa8d5d991217dc74d04e3f47d.png)\nThe matrix of the quadratic form ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/d4ecb15785c7b91e8596dd5ee6d5f4f37bf8021c5be668ec618955d401d4818f.png) is given above. What is the value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/5076087e153b1b98d9b1798601bd9f4fb4858085d9fd7b5695ee28d0ec82383c.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/8645c292302b7edfc416cf5ca509325a6ee9381fb231a7f2b159803b4dfda807.png)\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must do the following splits:\n\n- we split the coefficient of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/dfb385bea2635645b1f9c86af71eff0dce97a954417745dbd38490f018f08e0a.png) between the entries ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/6a348fce74db828ec978c7e135e99593bc998bfabecec36ecaf759cc06dba537.png) and\n\n- we split the coefficient of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/0ce406288d4b63c3156067f4ff753a5fec13d4461f11cf58252a1361f16b6911.png) between the entries ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/c24c0fe76b0f877030d6130109d0b82ef187e05be9c103d8b913b9c3eb654200.png)\n\nSo, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/e8fda0676083681fa61f11e26ca5455e06cf93ce11b657f7e1b46be3c30ff899.png)\n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/29e111e47c4fb83d1a5be9b51f83e463770c5c5d7a99eae453281f617e34fe86.png) ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/d6faa78e35bd56fb2a138698ca72569d54c7da3305c3bb5b9dfafd8662d49d7a.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/a8c65541492f0454624e520d1b86952208a1206735718dd49b7455f003d2bce5.png) Finally, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/851f6d6822dca779fa17406a68c7e6fbce37cf2642ce5994f8e95ede41e31921.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
